# State access

## Context

`selectors.ts` holds derived reads; `actions.ts` holds dispatchable writes.

## Rule

- Read state via `selectors.ts` functions, not inline `state.tasks` filtering.
- Write state via an `actions.ts` creator + `store.dispatch(...)`, never a
  hand-built `{ type, payload }` object elsewhere.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rn "state.tasks.filter|state.tasks.map" app/src` → matches only in
   `selectors.ts`.
2. `grep -rn '{ type: "' app/src` → matches only in `actions.ts`/`reducer.ts`/
   `types.ts`.
